I've been investigating the HP Remaining 0/0 bug and found the root cause:

**Root Cause of HP Remaining 0/0 Bug:**
In `src/handlers/combat-handler.js`, the `finalizeCombatState()` function (used for all player actions like PLAYER_ATTACK, PLAYER_ABILITY, etc.) **never calls `finalizeCombatStats()`** — it only merges overrides and calls `trackAchievements()`. Meanwhile, `finalizeCombatStats()` IS called properly inside `handleEnemyTurnLogic()`, but NOT when the player kills the enemy on their turn.

This means when the player lands the killing blow, `combatStats.finalPlayerHp` stays at 0 (default), producing the "0/0 (0%)" display.

**Fix:** In `finalizeCombatState()`, add a check for victory/defeat phase and call `finalizeCombatStats()` there:
```javascript
function finalizeCombatState(next, overrides = {}) {
  if (!next) return next;
  const combined = { ...next, ...overrides };
  const cs = combined.combatStats;
  if (cs && (combined.phase === 'victory' || combined.phase === 'defeat')) {
    finalizeCombatStats(cs, combined.phase, combined.player?.hp ?? 0, combined.player?.maxHp ?? 100);
    combined.combatStatsSummary = formatCombatStatsDisplay(cs);
  }
  return trackAchievements(combined);
}
```

